{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980165395,"sessionID":"ses_1cc872ecdffen9fSzPte8FNwPU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_78qa7v9ty3XaSAA9EyMHwqE4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Implemented issue #9493 by updating `MONDO:0005709` (`common cold`) in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`.\n2: \n3: Changes made:\n4: - Added `is_a: MONDO:0005550 ! infectious disease` to classify common cold under infectious disease.\n5: - Added provenance to that new parent axiom with:\n6:   - `source=\"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9493\"`\n7:   - `source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2955-4640\"`\n8: - Updated `property_value: IAO:0000233` from the previous issue link to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9493` so the edited term points back to the current curation request.\n9: \n10: Rationale:\n11: - The issue requested adding `infectious disease` as a parent for `common cold`.\n12: - The thread explicitly asked to implement the asserted parent addition without adding a logical definition.\n13: - The existing text definition already states that common cold is usually caused by viruses, so the added asserted parent is consistent with the term content.\n14: \n15: Checks completed:\n16: - [x] Read imported issue context and curator instructions.\n17: - [x] Inspected the existing `MONDO:0005709` and `MONDO:0005550` stanzas.\n18: - [x] Applied a minimal asserted-parent edit only.\n19: - [x] Verified ontology syntax locally with:\n20:   - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n21: - [ ] Ran ODK normalization (`make NORM`) and Docker-based validation.\n22: \n23: Validation note:\n24: - `robot convert` succeeded with no errors.\n25: - I could not run `sh run.sh make NORM` or the equivalent Docker-based ODK workflow in this environment because `docker` is not installed (`docker: command not found`).\n26: \n27: Commit:\n28: - `5e08065` `Add infectious disease parent to common cold`\n\n(End of file - total 28 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Implemented issue #9493 by updating `MONDO:0005709` (`common cold`) in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`.\n\nChanges made:\n- Added `is_a: MONDO:0005550 ! infectious disease` to classify common cold under infectious disease.\n- Added provenance to that new parent axiom with:\n  - `source=\"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9493\"`\n  - `source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2955-4640\"`\n- Updated `property_value: IAO:0000233` from the previous issue link to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9493` so the edited term points back to the current curation request.\n\nRationale:\n- The issue requested adding `infectious disease` as a parent for `common cold`.\n- The thread explicitly asked to implement the asserted parent addition without adding a logical definition.\n- The existing text definition already states that common cold is usually caused by viruses, so the added asserted parent is consistent with the term content.\n\nChecks completed:\n- [x] Read imported issue context and curator instructions.\n- [x] Inspected the existing `MONDO:0005709` and `MONDO:0005550` stanzas.\n- [x] Applied a minimal asserted-parent edit only.\n- [x] Verified ontology syntax locally with:\n  - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778980165367,"end":1778980165393}},"id":"prt_e337b16f3001UWGNJQM47TpG24","sessionID":"ses_1cc872ecdffen9fSzPte8FNwPU","messageID":"msg_e337b0740001MJVWKMInU91JJK"}}
